//RS // ── D-I9 `core.files`: one arm per Prelude symbol, no second spelling ──────
//RS // Every helper below is pure marshalling: it hands the resolved path to the
//RS // `jet_std_fs_*` symbol AOT emits and projects that symbol's `IOError` with
//RS // the shared `io_error_ct`. `Ok`/`Err` stay Rust-shaped here so the caller
//RS // decides the outcome carrier for its own row.
//RS pub(super) type FsResult<T> = Result<T, crate::AST::CtValue>;
